<?xml version="1.0"?>
<section xml:id="flask_static">
  <title>Static Files</title>
  <p>Dynamic web applications also need static files.  That's usually where
the CSS and JavaScript files are coming from.  Ideally your web server is
configured to serve them for you, but during development Flask can do that
as well.  Just create a folder called <c>static</c> in your package or next to
your module and it will be available at <c>/static</c> on the application.</p>

<p>To generate URLs for static files, use the special <c>'static'</c> endpoint name:</p>

  <pre>url_for('static', filename='style.css')</pre>

<p>The file has to be stored on the filesystem as <c>static/style.css</c>.</p>


</section>